    <briefdescription>
<para>Timeout guard for GPU backend operations. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Ensures all GPU dispatch operations complete within a bounded time envelope. If a GPU operation exceeds the timeout, the dispatcher silently falls back to the CPU path and records the incident for diagnostic purposes.</para>
<para>Contract per <ref refid="geo__api__contract_8h" kindref="compound">geo_api_contract.h</ref> §2:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Backend selection latency must not exceed kBackendSelectionBudget (100µs)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>GPU fallback must be silent (no error logged to user)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Result consistency must be preserved (CPU and GPU produce equivalent results)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread safety: const methods are thread-safe; state is immutable after construction. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
